From 243054ddac01f2ef9ff3f4fe20bd321fa4fb36d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:36:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): carry landing disposition through release,
 notices and payload [daveey]

Review of the landing gate (PR #636) found five gaps:
- observe_owner_task released origin sessions only on classification
  success, so an accepted CLOSED disposition never released them.
- The left-open notice was rendered only by the gateway formatter; the TUI
  formatter, its FINAL SEND early return and the remote completion text
  (which reuses it) dropped the reason and the hub-batch caveat.
- A malformed metadata.published_pr (int/list/non-URL string) on a
  local-only card surfaced as an infra retry or a misleading
  persisted-contract mismatch.
- The completed payload copied raw pr_left_open/landing_owner metadata, so
  a MERGED PR could announce "left open" and store an arbitrary owner.
- Guidance did not steer review-only cards away from published_pr, which
  binds the card's contract permanently.

Fixes: accept ok CLOSED receipts as contract evidence; render the left-open
notice in _kb_completed and the FINAL SEND branch; refuse non-URL
published_pr before any GitHub read as malformed_published_pr; derive
payload landing fields only from the recorded receipt['landing']; tell
review-only cards to use metadata.pr / metadata.reviewed_pr (prompt,
kanban_complete schema, docs).

RED: 14 of the new tests failed on 34fe22e1f16. GREEN: 26 new tests in
tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pr_landing_notices.py; 432 passed, 1 skipped
across 21 targeted files; scripts/check --base origin/main: 15 checks ok.
